# Every direction of walking on flat ground, in turn, with a pause between: ahead,
# backwards, to the left, to the right, ahead and to the left at once, then
# turning (the facing changes, the throttle stays ahead). The speeds of the
# directions are the tags' own and differ.
scenario walk_directions
map bloodgulch
# <name> <x> <y> <z> <yaw, radians>: a little above the ground, so that the
# player settles on it in the first ticks
start flat_field 77.9 -166.2 0.32 0.0
# (it ends before the walk reaches a scenery object that the engine bumps
# into and the simulation, which has the collision BSP alone, does not know)
ticks 520
input 30 90 forward=1.0
input 120 180 forward=-1.0
input 210 270 strafe=1.0
input 300 360 strafe=-1.0
input 390 450 forward=1.0 strafe=1.0
input 480 520 forward=1.0 yaw=1.0

# what the Rust simulation may differ from the C engine by: what walking on
# the ground reaches (its port of the engine's movement differs only by the
# rounding of its own square root, sine and cosine: at most 6e-5 world units
# and 4e-4 world units a second in the runs of these scenarios), with room
# for another machine's; a run of the C engine against itself allows none
tolerance position 0.001
tolerance velocity 0.005
tolerance facing 0.001
tolerance state 0
